unit('COUNTRIES','Pays, capitales, langues et monnaies',['Read country/capital/currency reference entries in French.','Distinguish a language community from legal official-language status.','Use nationality adjectives and dated source attribution.'],'''Francophone describes a person or community using French; anglophone concerns English. Neither label proves that everyone in a country speaks that language, or that it is the country’s only official language. Membership of an international organisation is another separate fact. The source’s two country lists should not be memorised as exclusive language classifications.
For example, the cited Côte d’Ivoire country profile identifies French as an official language; the Nigeria and Gambia profiles identify English. This does not erase their other languages. The OIF’s 2026 report describes multilingual use, including French and English in Cameroon and Rwanda. Check the date of a legal language-status statement; usage and legal status are not interchangeable.
Reference entries below cover the countries named in the original lesson without retaining its mistaken grouping. Format: country — capital recorded by UNData — currency name/code as recorded in its English profile. Access date: 27 October 2026. A currency code helps distinguish currencies with similar names; it is not an exchange rate.
'''+country_table+'''
Capital qualifications matter. UNData distinguishes Porto-Novo, the constitutional capital of Benin, from Cotonou, its economic capital. It names Yamoussoukro as Côte d’Ivoire’s capital and Abidjan as its administrative capital. For South Africa it distinguishes administrative Pretoria, legislative Cape Town and judicial Bloemfontein. The source’s Zaïre is not the present country name used in the reference table; use République démocratique du Congo and distinguish it from République du Congo.
French nationality adjectives agree with the person: nigérian/nigériane, ghanéen/ghanéenne, égyptien/égyptienne. Je suis nigériane; il est ghanéen. The source’s Nigerian, Egyptian and Ghanian are not the French forms required by this exercise.
Ask Quelle est la capitale du Ghana ? Answer La capitale du Ghana est Accra. Ask Quelle est la monnaie du Nigéria ? Answer C’est le naira. To report a head of state, include the dated source: the France Diplomatie Nigeria profile updated 17 June 2026 names Bola Ahmed Tinubu. This is a dated example, not an indefinitely current quiz answer. Recheck official records before setting a later current-affairs exercise.''',[q('Give the capitals of Burundi, Côte d’Ivoire and Ghana from the reference.','Gitega ; Yamoussoukro ; Accra.','Gitega','Yamoussoukro','Accra'),q('Why should the original country list not be treated as a list of countries with only one language?','A language may be used alongside others; usage, official status and international membership are different facts.','Multilingualism','Distinguishes use from official status'),q('Complete for a girl from Nigeria and a boy from Ghana: Elle est __. Il est __.','nigériane ; ghanéen.','nigériane','ghanéen'),q('Give Nigeria’s currency and explain why a head-of-state answer needs a date.','Naira (NGN). Office-holders can change, so name the reference date and check a current official record.','Naira/NGN','Change over time','Dated reference')],[(x['url'],'United Nations Statistics Division country profile: '+n) for n,x in zip(country_names,country_facts)]+[('https://www.diplomatie.gouv.fr/fr/information-par-pays/nigeria/presentation-du-nigeria','France Diplomatie: Nigeria, updated 17 June 2026'),('https://www.diplomatie.gouv.fr/fr/information-par-pays/gambie/presentation-de-la-gambie','France Diplomatie: Gambia, updated 11 May 2026'),('https://www.diplomatie.gouv.fr/fr/information-par-pays/cote-d-ivoire/presentation-de-la-cote-d-ivoire','France Diplomatie: Côte d’Ivoire, updated 3 June 2026'),('https://www.francophonie.org/sites/default/files/2026-03/La_langue_francaise_dans_le_monde_Edition_2026.pdf','OIF: La langue française dans le monde, edition 2026, multilingual institutional usage')])

